# Reactive Markdown

This page opts into the runtime because it declares state. Static pages ship zero framework JavaScript.

:state count = 0

The count is { count }.

:button "Increment" -> count++

:state open = false

:button "Show details" -> open = true
:button "Hide details" -> open = false

:if open
The details are visible now.
:else
The details are hidden.
:endif

## Keyed loops over real objects

The same `@loop` that unrolls static data also drives reactive lists. Items are objects, bindings use dotted paths, and the runtime patches the list by key instead of re-rendering it:

:state todos = [{"id": 1, "title": "Route pages", "owner": "PM"}, {"id": 2, "title": "Ship tiny runtime", "owner": "Dev"}]

@loop todos into todo
- **{ todo.title }** — { todo.owner }
@endloop

:button "Add todo" -> todos += {"id": 3, "title": "Live compile", "owner": "Testing"}

## Conditionals inside a loop, nested

`:if` works per row, and conditionals nest — the inner branch is decided after the outer one, for every item, and stays reactive. Add a "done" task and watch which badge each row shows:

:state tasks = [{"id": 1, "title": "Draft the spec", "done": true, "blocked": false}, {"id": 2, "title": "Wire the runtime", "done": false, "blocked": true}, {"id": 3, "title": "Write the demo", "done": false, "blocked": false}]

@loop tasks into task
::: card .task-row
**{ task.title }** —
:if task.done
done ✓
:else
:if task.blocked
blocked ✗
:else
in progress …
:endif
:endif
:::
@endloop

:button "Add a finished task" -> tasks += {"id": 4, "title": "Ship it", "done": true, "blocked": false}

Each row picks one of three states from two nested conditionals, all in plain Markdown — no component, no ternary, no JavaScript.

## Section-scoped state

Two sections can each own a state value named `tally` without colliding. Buttons resolve to the nearest scope:

::: section #left .tally-card
:state tally = 0

### Left section

The left tally is { tally }.

:button "Bump left" -> tally++
:::

::: section #right .tally-card
:state tally = 10

### Right section

The right tally is { tally }.

:button "Bump right" -> tally++
:::

Static pages like the docs stay runtime-free.

</main>
